## Two-tier mental model

```
   Product layer (long-lived, audience-facing)
   ├── 01-product/    — "what the product does for users"
   ├── 02-business/   — "how the business uses it"
   ├── 03-technical/  — "how it is built and integrated"
   └── 05-releases/   — "what shipped when"
                  ▲
                  │  promotes via Product Delta at slice close
                  │
   Project layer (short-lived, internal)
   └── 04-project/   — "what we're working on right now"
```

A **project** is a bounded development cycle (quarter, sprint cycle).
The **product** outlives the project. Each project consumes the product
baseline as input and proposes deltas back as output.

## Read order

- **New to the product?** Start at [01-product/](./01-product/) for what
  it does. Then [02-business/](./02-business/) for how the business uses it.
- **About to write code?** Read [03-technical/](./03-technical/) for the
  durable architecture, then [04-project/](./04-project/) for what's
  currently in flight.
- **Need to know what shipped?** [05-releases/](./05-releases/).

